{
  "title": "The order API runs in two zones and reaches menus, carts and keys over endpoints",
  "kicker": "Food delivery ordering backend · one region, two Availability Zones",
  "lede": "Amazon CloudFront takes orders from the apps and sits outside every region. Behind it, the order API runs as AWS Fargate tasks in both zones and writes orders to an Amazon RDS primary with a standby in the second zone. Menus in Amazon S3, carts in Amazon DynamoDB and the API's keys in AWS Secrets Manager are regional services the VPC reaches over endpoints, never addresses inside it.",
  "foot": "Illustrative topology · hop facts are placeholders, not looked-up values",
  "width": 1440,
  "badge": "Customer",
  "grammar": "aws",
  "body": [
